<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Cool, wet weather boosts crops.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Cool, wet weather boosts crops.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat movement was extremely slow early Tuesday with talk centered on improving crop prospects in Kansas, dealers said.</p>
<p>They noted rains had helped crop prospects in moisture-starved northwest Kansas while cool temperatures were giving freeze damaged crops in southern Kansas time to develop their limited potential.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we are behind in maturity which should help crops which suffered freeze damage,&quot; one southern Kansas dealer said.  </p>
